{"id":"adeb1236931d5593","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-l-series.md","title":"Local Zeta Function of a Finite-Field Projective Variety","display":"df-l-series — Local Zeta Function of a Finite-Field Projective Variety","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-l-series","aliases":["58-df-l-series","Local Zeta Function of a Variety"],"display":"df-l-series — Local Zeta Function of a Finite-Field Projective Variety","depends_on":["[[58-df-finite-field-projective-variety]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-l-series"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-l-series</span><span>Local Zeta Function of a Variety</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-l-series — Local Zeta Function of a Finite-Field Projective Variety"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e85b3308cfc79da5\" href=\"?note=e85b3308cfc79da5\" title=\"58-df-finite-field-projective-variety\">58-df-finite-field-projective-variety</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X=\\langle\\mathbb F_q,n,I,f\\rangle\">\\(X=\\langle\\mathbb F_q,n,I,f\\rangle\\)</span> is a projective-variety presentation with displayed homogeneous generator map <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb F_q\">\\(\\mathbb F_q\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N_X(r)=|X(\\mathbb F_{q^r})|\">\\(N_X(r)=|X(\\mathbb F_{q^r})|\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProjectiveVarietyPresentation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ProjectiveVarietyPresentation}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> are supplied by the dependencies.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LocalZetaSeries}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LocalZetaSeries}_S\\)</span> is the predicate defined here.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S\\)</span> is the point-count function predicate defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}local\\text{-}zeta\\text{-}point\\text{-}counts}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S(N,X,\\mathbb F_q,q,n,I,f)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveVarietyPresentation}_S(X,\\mathbb F_q,n,I,f)\\land\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S(\\mathbb F_q,q)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(N,\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\},\\omega)\\land\n\\forall r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;N(r)=|X(\\mathbb F_{q^r})|\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}local\\text{-}zeta\\text{-}point\\text{-}counts}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S(N,X,\\mathbb F_q,q,n,I,f)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveVarietyPresentation}_S(X,\\mathbb F_q,n,I,f)\\land\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S(\\mathbb F_q,q)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(N,\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\},\\omega)\\land\n\\forall r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;N(r)=|X(\\mathbb F_{q^r})|\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}l\\text{-}series}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LocalZetaSeries}_S(Z,X,\\mathbb F_q,q)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists n,I,f,N\\;\\left(\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S(N,X,\\mathbb F_q,q,n,I,f)\\land Z\\in\\mathbb Q⟦ t⟧\\land\nZ=\\exp\\!\\left(\\sum_{r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\\frac{N(r)}{r}t^r\\right)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}l\\text{-}series}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LocalZetaSeries}_S(Z,X,\\mathbb F_q,q)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists n,I,f,N\\;\\left(\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S(N,X,\\mathbb F_q,q,n,I,f)\\land Z\\in\\mathbb Q⟦ t⟧\\land\nZ=\\exp\\!\\left(\\sum_{r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\\frac{N(r)}{r}t^r\\right)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The displayed series is the local zeta function, not a general global <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-series.</li>\n<li>The rational-point sets are determined by the homogeneous presentation from the dependency, so the coefficients are finite integers.</li>\n<li>Presentation data and the point-count function are existentially bound inside the public zeta-series predicate; no free <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n,I,f\">\\(n,I,f\\)</span>, or <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N_X\">\\(N_X\\)</span> can change its truth value.</li>\n<li>Cohomological determinant factorization is a theorem following from the trace formula.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Milne, Etale Cohomology</li>\n<li>Serre, Zeta and L Functions</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-finite-field-projective-variety","status":"resolved","id":"e85b3308cfc79da5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-finite-field-projective-variety]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X=\\langle\\mathbb F_q,n,I,f\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"f","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb F_q","display":false},{"tex":"r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"N_X(r)=|X(\\mathbb F_{q^r})|","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ProjectiveVarietyPresentation}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LocalZetaSeries}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}local\\text{-}zeta\\text{-}point\\text{-}counts}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S(N,X,\\mathbb F_q,q,n,I,f)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{ProjectiveVarietyPresentation}_S(X,\\mathbb F_q,n,I,f)\\land\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S(\\mathbb F_q,q)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(N,\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\},\\omega)\\land\n\\forall r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;N(r)=|X(\\mathbb F_{q^r})|","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}l\\text{-}series}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LocalZetaSeries}_S(Z,X,\\mathbb F_q,q)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists n,I,f,N\\;\\left(\\mathrm{PointCountFunction}_S(N,X,\\mathbb F_q,q,n,I,f)\\land Z\\in\\mathbb Q⟦ t⟧\\land\nZ=\\exp\\!\\left(\\sum_{r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\\frac{N(r)}{r}t^r\\right)\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"n,I,f","display":false},{"tex":"N_X","display":false}],"bytes":2135,"backlinks":[{"id":"789230403cc61bdd","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-751","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-l-series.md|58-df-l-series]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["e85b3308cfc79da5","36d7463d215be751"]}